---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Terminal from "../components/Terminal.astro";

const repo = "https://github.com/jitendravjh/ghdeck";

const termHtml = `<span class="c"><b class="brand-tab">ghdeck</b></span>  <span class="tabs"><b>ATTENTION NEEDED [4]</b>  OPEN [8]  YOURS [46]  TO REVIEW [0]  ALL [50]</span>
<span class="sel"><span class="d"> 2h</span>  <span class="b">[PR]   </span> <span class="rp">screenpipe/screenpipe#6449</span>  <span class="t">fix(meetings): lock live transcription language</span>
             <span class="g">● open</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="r">✖ ci</span>   <span class="d">6 comments   jitendravjh commented</span></span>
<span class="d">╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌</span>
<span class="d"> 3d</span>  <span class="c">[ISSUE]</span> <span class="rp">JuliaEarth/CoordRefSystems.jl#315</span>  <span class="t">Add support for ESPG:28992</span>
             <span class="r">✖ closed</span>   <span class="d">9 comments   jitendravjh commented</span>
<span class="d">╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌</span>
<span class="d"> 3d</span>  <span class="b">[PR]   </span> <span class="rp">JuliaEarth/CoordRefSystems.jl#373</span>  <span class="t">Add EPSG code for Amersfoort / RD New</span>
             <span class="m">✔ merged</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="g">✔ approved</span>   <span class="d">1 comment   juliohm approved</span>
<span class="d">╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌</span>
<span class="d"> 5d</span>  <span class="b">[PR]   </span> <span class="rp">JuliaGeometry/Meshes.jl#1428</span>  <span class="t">Add conversion between azimuths and tangents</span>
             <span class="m">✔ merged</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="g">✔ approved</span>   <span class="d">3 comments   juliohm approved</span>
<span class="d">╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌</span>
<span class="d">3mo</span>  <span class="b">[PR]   </span> <span class="rp">SciML/NeuralOperators.jl#134</span>  <span class="t">feat: implement CNO (closes #122)</span>
             <span class="g">● open</span> <span class="d">·</span> <span class="r">! conflict</span>   <span class="d">2 comments   jitendravjh commented</span>
<span class="hr">────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>
<span class="u">https://github.com/screenpipe/screenpipe/pull/6449</span>
<span class="mt">by jitendravjh   +255 -17 in 3 files</span>
<span class="d">↑↓ move · ←→ filter · enter read · o open · r sync · / search · ? help · q quit</span>`;
const structuredData = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
    name: "ghdeck",
    applicationCategory: "DeveloperApplication",
    operatingSystem: "macOS, Linux",
    description:
      "A terminal dashboard for GitHub. PRs and issues in one list, newest first, with conflicts, CI and review state on every row.",
    url: "https://ghdeck.jitendravjh.in/",
    downloadUrl: `${repo}/releases`,
    license: "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT",
    author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Jitendra Verma" },
    offers: { "@type": "Offer", price: "0", priceCurrency: "USD" },
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout structuredData={structuredData}>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>All your GitHub work in one list.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      PRs and issues together, newest first, with conflicts, failing CI and who
      you are waiting on visible without opening anything.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="/docs/#install">Install ghdeck</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
    </div>

    <Terminal title="ghdeck" html={termHtml} />
    <p class="caption">
      An issue closing and the pull request that closed it, next to each other.
      That is the thing no other tool does.
    </p>

    <div class="install-big">
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <p>macOS and Linux. One line, then you are done.</p>
      <pre class="block">brew install jitendravjh/tap/ghdeck</pre>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/docs/#setup">Connect your account</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/#install">Other ways to install</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>GitHub splits this across two pages.</h2>
      <p>
        And neither one tells you if a pull request is conflicting or if CI has
        gone red. Other terminal dashboards keep PRs and issues in separate
        tabs. This one does not.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>One list</h3>
        <p>PRs and issues interleaved, newest first. Filter to what needs you, what is open, what is yours, what waits on your review.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Status that GitHub hides</h3>
        <p>Merge conflicts, CI rollup, review decisions and requested reviewers. GitHub search cannot even query conflicts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Read the thread</h3>
        <p>Press enter for the body, comments and reviews, with line comments under the review that made them. Bots collapse to one line.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Watches itself</h3>
        <p>Polls notifications with a conditional request. GitHub does not count 304s, so a quiet minute costs nothing at all.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Opens instantly</h3>
        <p>Everything sits in SQLite. The dashboard shows cached data straight away and syncs behind you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>One small binary</h3>
        <p>About 2 MB, nothing to install alongside it. Static on Linux, so any distro works.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Documentation.</h2>
      <p>Short pages for installing, connecting your account, and living in it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <a class="doc-link" href="/docs/#install">
        <h3>Install</h3>
        <p>Homebrew, or a prebuilt binary for your platform. Nothing to compile.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="doc-link" href="/docs/#setup">
        <h3>Setup</h3>
        <p>Sign in with gh, or set a token with the repo scope. Nothing else to configure.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="doc-link" href="/docs/#use">
        <h3>Use</h3>
        <p>Filters, keys, reading a thread, and the commands that print to stdout.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
